    # About Me
    Currently, I am working as a research scholar under the guidance 
    of [Prof. Srinivas Aluru](http://www.ee.iastate.edu/~aluru/). 
    Before this gig, I used to work as a software engineer in a 
    consultancy company for eight and half years. I customized, maintained 
    and developed software that manages product life cycle. While working 
    as a software engineering, I studied M.Tech. in Computer Science 
    and Engineering from [IIIT, Hyderabad](http://www.iiit.ac.in/). 
    Sometime during the first year of this century, I graduated from 
    [PSG College of Technology](http://www.psgtech.edu/)
    with a B.E. in Mechanical Engineering. A summary of my past life 
    is [here](http://www.linkedin.com/in/srirampc).

    I have a personal blog [here](http://srirampc.blogspot.com). But I
    rarely update it now a days. You can follow me
    [here](http://www.twitter.com/srirampc) on twitter!

    # About This Site
    I created this site after joining IIT Bombay as research scholar. The 
    primary goal of this site is to document my work/life in 
    IIT Bombay.
    This site was created using static website generator 
    [nanoc](http://nanoc.stoneship.org). It is built from the
    [nancoc blog](https://github.com/mgutz/nanoc3_blog) starter kit
    developed by [mgutz](http://github.com/mgutz).
    The HTML content is generated from a set of [haml](http://haml-lang.com/)
    and [markdown](http://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/) 
    files, while CSS is generated from [sass](http://sass-lang.com/) files.
    The use of simpler representation of content (i.e. markdown) enables 
    easier version control.

    The structure of the site is inspired from
    [Mark Reid](http://mark.reid.name/).
        

